  "rules": [
    "Apply a significant downward bias correction (approx. -10 to -12 EUR) to all forecast horizons when the immediate history shows a price decline from >65 EUR to <63 EUR, as the model fails to anticipate the subsequent crash to the 52-57 EUR range.",
    "Reduce forecast sensitivity to positive sentiment spikes (1.00) occurring during downtrends; the model incorrectly interprets these as reversal signals and projects a slow recovery, whereas the true outcome shows continued volatility and lower lows.",
    "Implement a 'lag correction' for the first 5-7 days of the forecast horizon: the model consistently overestimates prices by 2-4 EUR immediately following a drop, failing to capture the speed of the mean reversion to the 53-55 EUR floor.",
    "Adjust for 'overshoot' in the mid-term (days 10-20): when the model forecasts a gradual rise from the 52 EUR trough, reduce the projected slope by 50% as the actual market exhibits a slower, more volatile recovery pattern.",
    "Discard the model's long-term upward drift assumption (days 25-30) if the 18-day history ends with a sentiment score below 0.50; the model projects a steady climb to 62+ EUR, but the true outcome remains suppressed near 56-59 EUR."
  ]
